Fre3nder packages the Klipper/Moonraker runtime in companion mode against the
local Moonraker instance. The upstream installer,
system-service creation, package-manager integration and Moonraker git updater
are not used.

Fre3nder carries one narrow integration patch:
patches/0001-fre3nder-disable-system-config.patch

The patch removes OctoApp's Moonraker update-manager and allowed-service
integration from the local Moonraker host. The unused upstream
systemconfigmanager.py is omitted from the packaged runtime. Fre3nder's signed
.fre3app lifecycle remains the sole update and service-management path.

Python dependencies are locked separately in python-wheels.json. Pure-Python
wheels are downloaded and hash-verified on the build host. Pillow is copied
from the Fre3nder X2000 Buildroot output, where it is cross-built for the
hardware-qualified userspace ABI.

